@startuml Timing Synchronization
!theme plain
title Timing Synchronization Model
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE

participant "Frontend\n(Browser)" as browser
participant "Backend\n(Server)" as server
participant "LabJack\n(Hardware)" as labjack
database "Database" as db

== Clock Synchronization ==
browser -> server : GET /api/clock-sync
note over server : server_time = time.time()
server --> browser : {server_time, monotonic_ns}
note over browser
    Calculate offset:
    RTT = response_time - request_time
    offset = server_time - browser_time + (RTT/2)
end note

== Test Start - T0 ==
browser -> server : POST /api/sessions/{id}/video-start
note over server
    **T0 = command_start_timestamp**
    Record time when start command received
end note
server -> db : Store command_start_timestamp
server -> labjack : start_monitoring()
note over labjack
    Record monitoring_start_time
    Begin voltage streaming
end note
server --> browser : OK

== Video Presentation - T1 ==
browser -> browser : video.play()
note over browser
    **T1 = presentation_start**
    When first frame appears
    Use performance.now() for precision
end note
browser -> server : POST /api/lifecycle\n{event: VIDEO_START, timestamp: T1}
note over server
    **Presentation Delay = T1 - T0**
    Time for browser to render video
end note
server -> db : Store presentation_delay_ms

== Detection Timing ==
note over labjack
    Each detection has:
    - labjack_timestamp (hardware)
    - system_timestamp (Python time.time())
    - monotonic_ns (time.monotonic_ns())
end note

labjack -> db : Store detection_event

== Video Relative Calculation ==
note over server
    **video_relative_timestamp =**
    detection_timestamp - video_start_timestamp

    This aligns detection with video timeline
end note

== Drift Compensation ==
note over server
    Monitor clock drift over time:
    - Compare hardware vs system timestamps
    - Calculate drift_rate (ms/second)
    - Apply compensation to detection timestamps

    **drift_compensated_timestamp =**
    original_timestamp + (drift_rate * elapsed_time)
end note

== Latency Calculation ==
note over server #LightYellow
    **Latency Calculation:**

    1. Get detection video_relative_timestamp
    2. Find matching ground_truth timestamp
    3. latency_ms = (det_time - gt_time) * 1000

    **Positive latency:** Detection after GT (normal)
    **Negative latency:** Detection before GT (pre-trigger)
end note

== Timeline Alignment ==
note over browser #LightGreen
    **Frontend Correlation:**

    Ground Truth: frame_number → timestamp
    Detection: labjack_timestamp → video_relative

    Match using:
    - Direct: ±2 frames tolerance
    - Extended: ±5 frames (constant voltage)
end note

@enduml
